/target
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store

# The Scryfall payload cache that codegen and validate read: one JSON
# document per card in the pool, fetched from Scryfall's API and kept
# because their guidelines encourage caching. It is a cache of somebody
# else's data rather than source, and `docs/legal.md` §3 is why that line is
# kept sharp here instead of left to convenience — 1371 files of it were
# committed. CI restores it with `.github/actions/scryfall-cache` and
# `xtask` refetches whatever is missing, so nothing depends on it existing.
/data/scryfall-cache/
.idea/
# trunk default output (browser build of baylee-client)
dist/
# Bevy's on-disk web asset cache (Scryfall images, fetched at runtime)
.web-asset-cache/
# the gateway's card-art mirror (BAYLEE_ART_PATH). docs/legal.md §3: card
# images are cached at runtime and never committed.
art-cache/

# the gateway store of pictures a player uploads for a deck: its sleeve and
# its playmat (BAYLEE_DECK_IMAGE_PATH). Out of the repo for the same reason
# art-cache is, and because the tree already carries one untracked file that
# must never be committed.
deck-images/

# local configuration (see .env.example)
.env

# Claude Code: the skills under .claude/skills are project knowledge and are
# tracked; everything else in there is per-machine state.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/worktrees/
